From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: fmsh: add support for FM25S02A

The Fudan Micro FM25S02A is a 2 Gbit (256 MiB) SPI NAND built on the
same die family as the already supported FM25S01A, only with twice the
block count. Without the ID, the Ingenic ISVP-A1N USB-boot loader
reports:

    spi_nand flash@0: unknown raw ID a1 e5 a1 e5

and registers no MTD device, so DFU has no NAND to write to.

Geometry from the FM25S02A datasheet (Rev. 1.1): 2048-byte pages,
64-byte OOB, 64 pages per erase block (128 KiB), 2048 blocks total,
2 bits per cell, two planes of 1024 blocks. It shares the FM25S01A
single-bit-per-512-byte on-die ECC and its spare-area layout: the
2 KiB main area plus the first 16-byte chunks of OOB are ECC protected,
the OOB is fully user accessible except the bad-block marker in the
first byte, so the same ooblayout and cache variants are reused. The
datasheet guarantees a minimum of 2008 valid blocks, so the maximum
bad-block count is 40.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>

---
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/fmsh.c
@@ -62,6 +62,15 @@ static const struct spinand_info fmsh_spinand_table[] = {
 					      &update_cache_variants),
 		     0,
 		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&fm25s01a_ooblayout, NULL)),
+	SPINAND_INFO("FM25S02A",
+		     SPINAND_ID(SPINAND_READID_METHOD_OPCODE_DUMMY, 0xE5),
+		     NAND_MEMORG(1, 2048, 64, 64, 2048, 40, 1, 1, 1),
+		     NAND_ECCREQ(1, 512),
+		     SPINAND_INFO_OP_VARIANTS(&read_cache_variants,
+					      &write_cache_variants,
+					      &update_cache_variants),
+		     0,
+		     SPINAND_ECCINFO(&fm25s01a_ooblayout, NULL)),
 };
 
 static const struct spinand_manufacturer_ops fmsh_spinand_manuf_ops = {
-- 
